{
  "title": "Recognized on Sight",
  "image": "image.png",
  "narration": "narration.mp3",
  "bed": "music.mp3",
  "lines": [
    {
      "text": "Put a Catholic, a Baptist,\nand a Latter-day Saint"
    },
    {
      "text": "in one room"
    },
    {
      "text": "and ask them to describe\nJesus of Nazareth."
    },
    {
      "text": "The doctrines will differ."
    },
    {
      "text": "The portrait will not.",
      "gold": true
    },
    {
      "text": "Patient with the broken."
    },
    {
      "text": "Unafraid of the proud."
    },
    {
      "text": "Stopping for the one."
    },
    {
      "text": "His character is recognized\non sight"
    },
    {
      "text": "in every tradition\nthat names Him—",
      "gold": true
    },
    {
      "text": "and He said His people\nwould be known\nthe same way:"
    },
    {
      "text": "“By this shall all men know",
      "italic": true
    },
    {
      "text": "that ye are my disciples,",
      "italic": true
    },
    {
      "text": "if ye have love\none to another”",
      "italic": true,
      "ref": "John 13:35"
    },
    {
      "text": "Not by winning\nthe argument—"
    },
    {
      "text": "by the love.",
      "gold": true
    },
    {
      "text": "What unites us\nin Jesus Christ"
    },
    {
      "text": "runs deeper than anything\nthat divides us."
    },
    {
      "text": "There is a table set,"
    },
    {
      "text": "and a door left open.",
      "gold": true
    }
  ],
